cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Neuro-MINE
message: >-
  Analyze neuronal data and correlate it to behaviours and
  stimuli.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Danica
    family-names: Matovic
    email: matovic.5@osu.edu
    affiliation: The Ohio State University
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0001-8403-5141'
  - given-names: Martin
    family-names: Haesemeyer
    email: haesemeyer.1@osu.edu
    affiliation: The Ohio State University
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2704-3601'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/matovic5/neuro_mine'
abstract: >
  The Python package Neuro-MINE combines two
  machine-learning based modules: training and prediction.
  The training module links experimental predictors to
  neural activity recordings (e.g., functional imaging,
  electrophysiology) using a convolutional neural network.
  This allows capturing both linear and non-linear
  relationships while key aspects of these relationships are
  characterized using Taylor decomposition. The prediction
  module then allows users to compute the most likely neural
  response to hypothetical inputs, making it a powerful
  hypothesis generator when designing experimental plans. 

  For complete details on the architecture of Neuro-MINE,
  please refer to Costabile et al. (2023).
